 arg←opts Center arg;from;actions;units;∆where;∆size;∆extent;where;parent;psize;punits;Borders;where_extent;_size;t;_extent;stretch_;border_;extent_;size_;ps;extent
⍝ Generic routine to auto-center new objects on their parent by modifying the provided argument list before ∆WI execution
⍝ opts← namespace with optional controlling variables
⍝       parent: Reference to parent object [required]
⍝       stretch: Pretend new object is this many pixels bigger (vertical, horizontal) for centering calculations
⍝       border: Make sure the created object takes into account any requested borders
⍝       size: Override size creation with an explicit value
⍝ If this routine is not used during ∇New processing, be sure to at least set _where, _extent, & _size variables before calling ∇Initialize.

 from←⊃⎕RSI ⍝ Immediate source namespace calling me (where I can find my needed settings)
 actions←⊃¨⊆¨arg ⍝ The names of the actions that they've asked to create this object with
 parent←opts ⎕VGET'parent' ⍝ They have to tell us this, at least
 t←⌈/0,⍸⍤1⊢'where' 'size' 'extent'∘.≡actions ⍝ Locate the LAST occurance of each of these user-provided parameters?
 t[2 3]×←t[2 3]=⌈/t[2 3] ⍝ Ignore any sizing term that happens before the last occurrence of either
 (∆where ∆size ∆extent)←∊¨(⍬⊂⍛,1↓¨arg)[1+t] ⍝ Which of our defaults are they explicitly providing (so we can skip adding defaults)

 ⍝ If needed, modify or prepend a default 'where' for object creation
 :If 4≠≢where←∆where ⍝ If they're not giving us a full 4⍴ "where", generate a default they can modify later
     (punits units)←1 0 1/##.Classes._supp.MyUnits parent ⍝ Get the unit-conversions for the parent object's scale
     _size←from ⎕VGET⊂'_size'(1.5 10) ⍝ Look for a class-specified size, but default to a common size if not there
     _extent←from ⎕VGET⊂'_extent'⍬ ⍝ Look for a class-specified extent
     (stretch_ border_ extent_ size_)←opts ⎕VGET('stretch'(0 0))('border' 0)('extent'⍬)('size'⍬) ⍝ Obtain named optional parameters being passed in
     ⍝? Ok, if the size parameter is specified here then we also have to figure out what the scale is in use at the current point of the argument line.
     ⍝? However, so far, only the extent parameter is being used and that doesn't depend on the creation-argument line at all.
     ⍝? Watch out for this becoming a problem if we decide to use size in the future!
     'Can''t center with a size without checking for scale changes first!'##.Halt×≢size_
     ps←units[1;]÷punits ⍝ How to translate a size to an extent ⍝? Watch out for borders?
     ⍝ Compute the correct extent in priority order given all the different inputs
     :If 2≠≢extent←∆extent ⍝ First look to see if they provided an extent in the command line
     :AndIf 2≠≢extent←∆size×∆size≢⍛↑ps ⍝ Then check to see if they provided a size in the command line
     :AndIf 2≠≢extent←extent_ ⍝ Then look to see if an extent is passed from the ∇New function
     :AndIf 2≠≢extent←size_×size_≢⍛↑ps ⍝ Then look to see if a size is passed from the ∇New function
     :AndIf 2≠≢extent←_extent ⍝ Then see if we've got a class default extent
     :AndIf 2≠≢extent←_size×_size≢⍛↑ps ⍝ Then look to see if we've got a class default size
         ⍝ This can't ever get here because there will always at least be an assumed _size
     :EndIf
     Borders←##.Classes._supp.GetBorders(_Class:from ⋄ _border:border_) ⍝ Pass a temporary fake GUI namespace containing the needed variables
     where_extent←extent+punits÷⍨+/2 2⍴Borders[1;3;] ⍝ Add border-spacing between extent and where
     :If 2=≢where ⍝ If they've supplied a partial 'where' (2⍴), then just modify it in-place to append the extent to it
         arg←(⊂'where'(where,where_extent))@(actions⍳⊂'where')⊢arg
     :Else ⍝ Otherwise, prepend a full default value
         psize←parent._size ⍝ What is the parent's size (in punits)? ⍝? Does this give us the right data for scale=0 now?
         where←(2÷⍨|psize-where_extent+stretch_÷punits),where_extent ⍝ For some reason, some objects aren't exactly centered by default
         arg,⍨←⊂'where'where ⍝ [2] Start us with a default 'where' extent and position (APL+Win measure) -- will usually be overridden later
     :EndIf
     ⍝? We may also remove any existing 'extent' (or 'size') from their command line so we don't re-execute it? But is it worth it?
 :EndIf

 ⍝? We could have this preset Border as well, but it doesn't belong with centering and not all (just most) classes call this
